{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>And he shall make atonement for the house and it shall be clean.</b> Behold, this atonement is through the bird that is sent away, that the bird shall carry all his iniquities outside the city into the open field, like the manner of the atonement through the goat that is sent away. And because the punishment of the plague-mark that appears in a person's house is not like the punishment of the plague-mark on his body, Scripture did not require an asham and a sin-offering, for it is sufficient for him with the first atonement that the metzora brings for his purification, namely the birds and the cedar wood and the hyssop."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:53.699366482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}